                  <handDesc>
                     
                     <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                        <seg type="script">Hand a: mediocre; hand b: mediocre</seg>
                        <seg type="ink">Black, red (strong amaranth in <locus from="2r" to="3v">2r-3v</locus>, 148v; vivid red in <locus from="4r" to="148r">4r-148r</locus>)</seg>
                        Scribe: Gabra Dǝngǝl. The name of
                        the original scribe has been erased from the concluding supplication formula
                        on <locus target="#148ra">148ra</locus> and replaced with the name of ʾabbā
                        Gabra Dǝngǝl (who probably wrote Text I-1, hand a).<date>Hand a: 19th
                           century (?); hand b: 18th century (?)</date>
                        <list type="abbreviations">
                           <item>
                              <abbr>ምዕራ:</abbr> for <expan>ምዕራፍ: </expan> (<locus target="#95ra">95ra</locus>, 143va)</item>
                        </list>
                        <seg type="rubrication">Nomina sacra; two initial lines in the incipit of
                           Text I-1; a few groups of lines (alternating with black lines) on the
                           incipit page of Text I-2; incipits of miracles (sometimes alternating
                           with a black line); the words ʾǝsaggǝd “I worship” and la-malakotǝka “Thy
                           Godhead” in Text I-1; elements of the punctuation signs; elements of
                           Ethiopic numerals.</seg>
                     </handNote>
                     <handNote xml:id="h2" script="Ethiopic">Hand a: <locus from="2r" to="3v">2r-3v</locus> (ʾabba Gabra Dǝngǝl): the letters are slightly
                        right-sloping, tend to rectangular shapes, some with
                        hairlines.</handNote>
                     <handNote xml:id="h3" script="Ethiopic"> Hand b: <locus from="4r" to="149v">4r-149v</locus>: the letters are slightly left-sloping, broad, round,
                        some with
                        hairlines.</handNote>
                  </handDesc>
