               <provenance>Walda ʾIyasu is mentioned as the donor in
                     Additio 1 and at the end of Text I-1 (148vb).
                     His name and the names of his family members are written in a secondary hand,
                     over an erasure, in the concluding supplication formula on 148ra and in the supplication formulas: Walda ʾIyasu
                        (4ra, 22vb, 43va), Näṣḥa Dǝngǝl (4ra, 22vb), Rämḥa Śǝllāse (42vb, 47ra), Ḫiruta Śǝllāse (4ra,
                     12vb), Gabra ʾIyasus (4ra, 12vb), Walda Fāsiladas
                        (12vb), Walda Libānos (14va, 58ra), Walatta ʾAbiy ʾƎgziʾ (14va), Walatta Sänbät (29rb), Ḫāyla
                     Māryām (98rb). The name of the original owner, ʾabbā Yämanä Krǝstos, has been erased from the
                     supplication formulas but is still visible on 133ra, 148ra.</provenance></history>
